# Legacy sitemap URLs kept alive for Googlebot.
#
# They 301 to the CURRENT, versioned sitemap index so no crawler ever lands on
# the purged, frozen /sitemap-index.xml. That old index is intentionally removed
# at build time (removeStaleSitemapIndexes) so it returns 404 and Google drops
# its stale parse — see docs/indexing-recovery-2026-06.md §6. We deliberately do
# NOT redirect the bare /sitemap-index.xml here: it must 404 to force a fresh
# discovery pass on the new versioned URL.
#
# IMPORTANT: scripts/generate-programmatic-sitemaps.mjs rewrites the index-target
# lines below (in out/_redirects) to match SITEMAP_INDEX_NAME during the build,
# so bumping the sitemap version never silently re-breaks these legacy redirects.
/sitemap.xml            /sitemap-main-pages.xml            301
/sitemap_index.xml      /sitemap-index-2026-06-v2.xml      301
/sitemaps.xml           /sitemap-index-2026-06-v2.xml      301
